I can't add the `http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority and grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`. Adding HTTP would also send digest text in a URL query string to an external host, outside the capability the node was given. If the grant really is changing, that change should go through the graph definition and be reviewed before it takes effect. The implementation below uses only the notifier.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let mut message = format!("Digest {}\n{}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        for entry in composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept) {
            message.push_str(&format!("\n- {} ({})", entry.title, entry.link));
        }

        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

